// ── end r24.14 [REGIONS] switch readers ────────────────────────────────────────
// ── r24.13 [VISION] switch readers ─────────────────────────────────────────────
//    (r24.13 VISION insertions go directly below this line)
// ── r24.13 (WO-X1): the acuity drain's blocking window, opened and closed ─────
// What was wrong (ARCH §1.5 row 1, measured): a declared or acuity look holds
// the loop thread inside vision_drain_eval's wait for the JOB's own budget —
// stamped acuity_wait_ms = 120 s, and predict_vision_s(2040) = 48.0 s of real
// encode — and that wait polls only the encoder slot and g_stop_requested.
// The outage tape, which exists for exactly this, arms only around compaction
// (all four outage_mic sites are in compact_service), and both idle look-drain
// branches then run audio.clear(). So r24.12 opened a forty-eight-second deaf
// window ending in the ring being discarded, where r24.11's ceiling was one
// second. 31 Aug 13:54:57 — "you still have not activated the camera" — lands
// inside it and is lost.
//
// WHY A HOOK AND NOT AN ARM AT THE CALL SITE. The tape must cover the WAIT and
// nothing else. ALL THREE athena_vision_seam_drain call sites can play an
// announce ("I'm reading it — one moment.") from INSIDE that function, before
